@civic_fox58 Start with a small first issue, not a large feature. Give one clear maintainer contact and explain how reviews work. The README should cover local setup, tests, style, licence, and release rules.

Use a short contributor checklist. Include expected test command and a sample PR. New people often fail because hidden CI rules exist.

Also pin tool versions. “Works on my machine” is not onboarding. For dependencies, verify lockfiles and package signatures where possible.

