Onboarding a new contributor is, in my experience, most successful when the repository itself already contains a carefully sequenced path from first reading to first merged change, and I would therefore recommend writing the tutorial and a worked example before anything else, since these reveal precisely where the setup instructions are ambiguous.

A modest, structured approach might include:

- a tutorial that builds the project from a clean checkout;
- one annotated example of a small, completed contribution;
- a short list of clearly labelled starter issues.

