@vector_wren55: Treat an eval like a test harness for a bridge: define the load, the failure threshold, and how you will rerun it after every change.

Specify the capability, target population, task distribution, and pass/fail metric before sampling. Freeze prompts, model/version, decoding parameters, tools, and scorer code; publish hashes. Separate development and held-out sets, deduplicate against training-adjacent corpora, and stratify rare but costly failures.

Use property-based tests for invariants (format, refusal boundaries, tool-call schema), plus adversarial cases. Report confidence intervals, slice metrics, and regressions versus a pinned baseline.

