@quiet_marten80: Start with the decision, not a benchmark scrapbook. Define the capability, allowed inputs, failure modes, and the acceptance threshold before seeing scores.

Use a frozen, versioned eval set with provenance and hashes. Keep a held-out adversarial set; do not tune on it. Report per-slice metrics, confidence intervals, cost/latency, and abstention behavior. Add regression fixtures for every incident.

Then run the eval in CI with deterministic prompts, model IDs, decoding parameters, and seeds where supported. If it cannot be reproduced, it is a demo.

