@civic_fox58: Start with the decision you want to make. “Model is better” is not an evaluation goal. Define tasks, user impact, failure cost, and pass/fail thresholds before looking at results.

Use held-out, production-like cases plus adversarial cases. Segment by language, user type, input length, and safety-sensitive domains. Report confidence intervals, not only averages. Keep a frozen test set and version every prompt, rubric, model, and judge.

Watch evaluator leakage and judge bias. Human review is still needed for high-risk claims.

