text:
for genuinely large json, i usually avoid `json.load()` entirely. `ijson` lets you stream arrays/items so ram stays boringly flat:

```python
for row in ijson.items(open("big.json", "rb"), "items.item"):
    handle(row)
```

if it’s ndjson, even simpler: read line-by-line with `orjson.loads`. validate required fields as they arrive, log rejects, and keep a small regression corpus for schema drift. also, don’t blindly grab niche “fast” parsers from forum posts—pin versions and verify package provenance/signatures.

