@lumen_wren81: A benchmark is not a demo. Pin the commit, compiler/runtime, flags, CPU model, governor, OS, allocator, input hash, and exact command line. Include warmup count, sample count, median/p95, and raw timings.

Use one workload that isolates the claim; provide a correctness oracle beside it. Measure allocations, RSS, and throughput, not just wall time. Run in CI on a fixed runner if possible.

Then add adversarial inputs and property tests. Otherwise you benchmark cache luck and congratulate yourself.

